{"page":35,"verses":[{"verse_key":"2:220","surah":2,"ayah":220,"ar_uthmani":"فِى ٱلدُّنْيَا وَٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ ۗ وَيَسْـَٔلُونَكَ عَنِ ٱلْيَتَـٰمَىٰ ۖ قُلْ إِصْلَاحٌ لَّهُمْ خَيْرٌ ۖ وَإِن تُخَالِطُوهُمْ فَإِخْوَٰنُكُمْ ۚ وَٱللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ ٱلْمُفْسِدَ مِنَ ٱلْمُصْلِحِ ۚ وَلَوْ شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ لَأَعْنَتَكُمْ ۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"on this world and the next. They ask you about [the property of] orphans: say, ‘It is good to set things right for them. If you combine their affairs with yours, remember they are your brothers and sisters: God knows those who spoil things and those who improve them. Had He so willed, He could have made you vulnerable too: He is almighty and wise.’","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"فِى","en_gloss":"Concerning","transliteration":"fī","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":2,"ar":"ٱلدُّنْيَا","en_gloss":"the world","transliteration":"l-dun'yā","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":3,"ar":"وَٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ ۗ","en_gloss":"and the Hereafter","transliteration":"wal-ākhirati","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":4,"ar":"وَيَسْـَٔلُونَكَ","en_gloss":"They ask you","transliteration":"wayasalūnaka","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":5,"ar":"عَنِ","en_gloss":"about","transliteration":"ʿani","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":6,"ar":"ٱلْيَتَـٰمَىٰ ۖ","en_gloss":"the orphans","transliteration":"l-yatāmā","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":7,"ar":"قُلْ","en_gloss":"Say","transliteration":"qul","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":8,"ar":"إِصْلَاحٌۭ","en_gloss":"Setting right (their affairs)","transliteration":"iṣ'lāḥun","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":9,"ar":"لَّهُمْ","en_gloss":"for them","transliteration":"lahum","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":10,"ar":"خَيْرٌۭ ۖ","en_gloss":"(is) best","transliteration":"khayrun","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":11,"ar":"وَإِن","en_gloss":"And if","transliteration":"wa-in","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":12,"ar":"تُخَالِطُوهُمْ","en_gloss":"you associate with them","transliteration":"tukhāliṭūhum","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":13,"ar":"فَإِخْوَٰنُكُمْ ۚ","en_gloss":"then they (are) your brothers","transliteration":"fa-ikh'wānukum","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":14,"ar":"وَٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"And Allah","transliteration":"wal-lahu","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":15,"ar":"يَعْلَمُ","en_gloss":"knows","transliteration":"yaʿlamu","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":16,"ar":"ٱلْمُفْسِدَ","en_gloss":"the corrupter","transliteration":"l-muf'sida","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":17,"ar":"مِنَ","en_gloss":"from","transliteration":"mina","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":18,"ar":"ٱلْمُصْلِحِ ۚ","en_gloss":"the amender","transliteration":"l-muṣ'liḥi","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":19,"ar":"وَلَوْ","en_gloss":"And if","transliteration":"walaw","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":20,"ar":"شَآءَ","en_gloss":"(had) willed","transliteration":"shāa","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":21,"ar":"ٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-lahu","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":22,"ar":"لَأَعْنَتَكُمْ ۚ","en_gloss":"surely He (could have) put you in difficulties","transliteration":"la-aʿnatakum","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":23,"ar":"إِنَّ","en_gloss":"Indeed","transliteration":"inna","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":24,"ar":"ٱللَّهَ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-laha","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":25,"ar":"عَزِيزٌ","en_gloss":"(is) All-Mighty","transliteration":"ʿazīzun","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":26,"ar":"حَكِيمٌۭ","en_gloss":"All-Wise","transliteration":"ḥakīmun","verse_key":"2:220"},{"pos":27,"ar":"٢٢٠","en_gloss":"(220)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"2:220"}]},{"verse_key":"2:221","surah":2,"ayah":221,"ar_uthmani":"وَلَا تَنكِحُوا۟ ٱلْمُشْرِكَـٰتِ حَتَّىٰ يُؤْمِنَّ ۚ وَلَأَمَةٌ مُّؤْمِنَةٌ خَيْرٌ مِّن مُّشْرِكَةٍ وَلَوْ أَعْجَبَتْكُمْ ۗ وَلَا تُنكِحُوا۟ ٱلْمُشْرِكِينَ حَتَّىٰ يُؤْمِنُوا۟ ۚ وَلَعَبْدٌ مُّؤْمِنٌ خَيْرٌ مِّن مُّشْرِكٍ وَلَوْ أَعْجَبَكُمْ ۗ أُو۟لَـٰٓئِكَ يَدْعُونَ إِلَى ٱلنَّارِ ۖ وَٱللَّهُ يَدْعُوٓا۟ إِلَى ٱلْجَنَّةِ وَٱلْمَغْفِرَةِ بِإِذْنِهِۦ ۖ وَيُبَيِّنُ ءَايَـٰتِهِۦ لِلنَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُونَ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Do not marry idolatresses until they believe: a believing slave woman is certainly better than an idolatress, even though she may please you. And do not give your women in marriage to idolaters until they believe: a believing slave is certainly better than an idolater, even though he may please you. Such people call [you] to the Fire, while God calls [you] to the Garden and forgiveness by His leave. He makes His messages clear to people, so that they may bear them in mind.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَلَا","en_gloss":"And (do) not","transliteration":"walā","verse_key":"2:221"},{"pos":2,"ar":"تَنكِحُوا۟","en_gloss":"[you] marry","transliteration":"tankiḥū","verse_key":"2:221"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ٱلْمُشْرِكَـٰتِ","en_gloss":"[the] polytheistic women","transliteration":"l-mush'rikāti","verse_key":"2:221"},{"pos":4,"ar":"حَتَّىٰ","en_gloss":"until","transliteration":"ḥattā","verse_key":"2:221"},{"pos":5,"ar":"يُؤْمِنَّ ۚ","en_gloss":"they believe","transliteration":"yu'minna","verse_key":"2:221"},{"pos":6,"ar":"وَلَأَمَةٌۭ","en_gloss":"And a bondwoman","transliteration":"wala-amatun","verse_key":"2:221"},{"pos":7,"ar":"مُّؤْمِنَةٌ","en_gloss":"(who is) believing","transliteration":"mu'minatun","verse_key":"2:221"},{"pos":8,"ar":"خَيْرٌۭ","en_gloss":"(is) better","transliteration":"khayrun","verse_key":"2:221"},{"pos":9,"ar":"مِّن","en_gloss":"than","transliteration":"min","verse_key":"2:221"},{"pos":10,"ar":"مُّشْرِكَةٍۢ","en_gloss":"a polytheistic woman","transliteration":"mush'rikatin","verse_key":"2:221"},{"pos":11,"ar":"وَلَوْ","en_gloss":"[and] even if","transliteration":"walaw","verse_key":"2:221"},{"pos":12,"ar":"أَعْجَبَتْكُمْ ۗ","en_gloss":"she pleases you","transliteration":"aʿjabatkum","verse_key":"2:221"},{"pos":13,"ar":"وَلَا","en_gloss":"And (do) not","transliteration":"walā","verse_key":"2:221"},{"pos":14,"ar":"تُنكِحُوا۟","en_gloss":"give in marriage (your women)","transliteration":"tunkiḥū","verse_key":"2:221"},{"pos":15,"ar":"ٱلْمُشْرِكِينَ","en_gloss":"(to) [the] polytheistic men","tr